<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<form name="frmWoD20_1" align="client" theme="dark">
	<scrollBox align="client">
		<!--
			Theme backdrop (SPEC T158). Declared FIRST so it paints behind the boxes, and
			hitTest="false" so it can never eat a click. It carries no field and no
			left/top/width/height: it is not part of the data contract and the gate keeps
			measuring the real boxes for overlap (SPEC V57).

			Hidden here and switched on only by a Victorian theme - and if the art is ever
			missing it simply stays hidden, which is a sheet without an ornament rather than
			a half-painted one (SPEC V56).

			The name carries the tab number because a control name is global across the
			sheet's files: eight tabs sharing one name killed the compile with no message at
			all (SPEC B19 / V59). The Lua matches on the prefix.
		-->
		<image name="themePaper1" align="client" style="stretch" hitTest="false" visible="false"/>

		<!--
			The clan, born ASLEEP (SPEC V173, T432): invisible AND disabled, and no Lua on any
			tab writes the field, so nothing can fill it. It exists now only so the roster of
			CLANS (SPEC I17) has one owner of `clan` the day a round wakes it up - and so V8
			closes, since a widget that is hidden is still a widget.

			Outside every box on purpose: it draws nothing, so it belongs to no layout and it
			cannot push a sibling around. Dimmed like every other read-only widget (SPEC V111)
			- unobservable while it is hidden, but the rule is about what the XML says.

			Sixty entries, the thirteen clans plus the bloodlines the core lists in its tenth
			chapter, with Gargoyles as four rows (SPEC I17). The empty first entry is the one
			every picker carries (SPEC V15).
		-->
		<comboBox name="cboClan" left="0" top="0" width="230" height="25" visible="false" enabled="false" field="clan"/>
		<!--
			Layout grid (SPEC T41, V26, V27). Everything closes on x=1345 / y=866.

			The bottom line moved 852 -> 878 in the 125th round and 878 -> 853 in the 141st, and
			both moves are the same rule: V69 reads all three bottom boxes closing on ONE y, so
			they travel together or the check reddens. The 125th GREW them 26 to seat the road
			picker over the dot track (SPEC I99i, user Q8); the 141st took 25 back, because Q27
			put the ROAD label on the picker's own line and the box no longer needs a title row
			(SPEC I99k, I99l).

			  header  0..1010      EXPERIENCE 1015..1345                y   0..105
			  ATTRIBUTES 0..340                                        y 110..406
			                       TALENTS 345..675 | SKILLS 680..1010 | KNOWLEDGES 1015..1345   y 110..536
			  avatar     0..340                                   y 411..785
			                       VIRTUES 345..675                    y 541..667
			                       ROAD + BEARING 680..1010            y 541..667
			                       WILLPOWER 680..1010                 y 672..785 (52nd batch; 56th: ROAD as tall as VIRTUES)
			                       HEALTH  1015..1345                  y 541..866 at ten rows

			That is the sheet AS AUTHORED, and since the 47th batch it is the MORTAL sheet (SPEC
			I190a, user 2026-10-01): ROAD sits between VIRTUES and HEALTH again. A VAMPIRE gets a
			different Main, and the XML cannot hold two - renderGameMode on the root moves the named
			boxes to VAMP_GEOM and back to these numbers (SPEC I190c, V534):

			  header  0..1010      EXPERIENCE 1015..1300                y   0..105   avatar 1305..1543  y 0..236
			  ATTRIBUTES 0..1300 (Physical | Social | Mental)          y 110..236
			  TALENTS 0..430 | SKILLS 435..865 | KNOWLEDGES 870..1300  y 241..592
			  VIRTUES 0..340 | ROAD 345..675 | BLOOD POOL 680..1010 | HEALTH 1015..1300   y 597..
			                   ROAD y 597..723, WILLPOWER (boxWillpower) y 728..841 under it

			The 48th batch (SPEC I191, user 2026-10-01) put the rotated group names back, each one
			before its third of the band, and took the 25px the headings used off the band; and the
			Main closes on KNOWLEDGES' edge, so EXPERIENCE and HEALTH are 285 there.

			The 50th batch (SPEC I193, user 2026-10-02) took one typed row off each ability column -
			ten names and two - so everything under them rose 25; the avatar went up beside
			EXPERIENCE at twice its height, VIRTUES took its place under TALENTS (ten wider, its rows
			re-centred by VAMP_GEOM) and ROAD, no longer stacked, closes up on the abilities.

			Nine dots a row is why the ability boxes are 430 there: the row grows by four dots and the
			box with it, pushing the next one along (SPEC Q109.2). Titles and rows that span a box
			carry anchors="left top right", so they stretch with it and no Lua walks them.

			Read it as a FOUR-BAND GRID, which is what V375 measures since T908: every box on
			the tab starts and ends on a band edge - 0/340, 345/675, 680/1010, 1015/1345 - with
			a 5px gutter between bands, and each box on the bottom row shares both x edges with
			the column above it. The FIFTH band lasted two days: the 157th round moved
			SPECIALTIES into the grid row beside KNOWLEDGES (SPEC I126) and T908 put it back
			under SKILLS, which is where V168 had it.

			44th batch (SPEC I187, user 2026-09-26): SPECIALTIES is GONE and ROAD took its place
			under SKILLS, at its own 184. The avatar closes where HEALTH closes at SEVEN levels -
			541 + 7 * HEALTH_ROW_PITCH + HEALTH_BOX_PAD = 785 - and HEALTH itself is only READ for
			it, never moved (SPEC V415, I187c).

			46th batch (SPEC I189c/d, user 2026-10-01): ROAD went back UNDER VIRTUES, a stack in
			the 345..675 band again (SPEC V393), and the band under SKILLS holds the BLOOD POOL of
			a vampire - shown only when the game is Vampire, closing on the same seven-level line
			as the avatar (SPEC V532). Any other game sees that band empty.

			The bottom row does not close on ONE line, and that is the ask rather than drift:
			VIRTUES and ROAD end on their own content plus the 15px foot (SPEC V393), the avatar
			on HEALTH's seven-row floor (SPEC V415) - while HEALTH alone ends at 866. Which box
			does NOT close the line is DERIVED from the V393 and V415 rosters and never typed into
			the gate - a box that quietly stops closing it leaves no other trace (SPEC V376,
			I136d, Q47, Q49).

			HEALTH being the ONLY closer is why V376 had to be re-formed in the same commit that
			moved the avatar (SPEC Q63, T939): an equality over one element is true for whatever
			height that element has, so the guard moved off the closers and onto the roster - if
			the names drain away there is nothing left to excuse, and three is the measured floor
			(SPEC B7, B145). The owner chose that shape deliberately: HEALTH is the one box on the
			sheet whose height is decided at RUNTIME (SPEC V49), so it cannot be pinned to a line
			the other three write into the XML.

			The 157th round traded HEIGHT for WIDTH - 891 -> 888 high and 1345 -> 1680 wide -
			and T908 gave the width back. The sheet does NOT shrink with it: TRAITS closes on
			1595 and always has, so it is the widest tab and popScrim measures the widest TAB
			rather than this box (SPEC V396, B127). The old rule tied the scrim to this box right
			edge; it was green while Main was WIDER than Traits, and leaving it would have cut
			the scrim to 1345 and left 250px of Traits unable to close the overlay (SPEC I136g,
			B124, B129).

			The line moved 853 -> 928 -> 895 in the 154th round and 895 -> 891 in the 155th.
			It went DOWN 75 because the ability columns went from twelve rows to FIFTEEN (SPEC
			I123, I123a) - seven names the user asked for, plus the typed rows that square the
			three columns off - and then back UP 33 when one vertical ruler of 25 replaced the
			three the tab had inherited: the header went 30 -> 25, VIRTUES 29 -> 25, SPECIALTIES
			30 -> 25 (SPEC I124, V370).

			The last 4 are VIRTUES opening its first row on the title HAIRLINE, which every other
			titled box on the tab already did and nothing was checking (SPEC V374, I125c). It is
			the only ruler slack the tab had left: the user asked for three boxes to shrink and
			I125 measured all ten, box by box - the other two were already at the floor, 20px of
			margin on four sides and rows that touch.

			SPECIALTIES used to carry that difference as FOLGA under its last row, until the owner
			aligned its floor to ROAD (SPEC V402) - and the 44th batch took the box out of the
			sheet altogether, V402 with it (SPEC I187a).

			The columns are 436 tall, not 340: fifteen rows from 41 at a pitch of 25 close at
			416, and the 20px under the last one is the margin ATTRIBUTES sets (SPEC V171). The
			height is DERIVED from the row count, so a sixteenth ability has to grow the box
			instead of moving into slack nobody declared.

			HEALTH used to be the one box that did not close on the bottom line, and since the
			157th round it is the box that SETS it. What is AUTHORED is the ten-row case, which
			ends at 896, and the renderer shrinks it to the chosen track length (SPEC V49); ROAD
			and the avatar close on 896 with it, so the overhang V69 let it off with is ZERO
			(SPEC V376). The number stays in the gate at 0 rather than being deleted: 0 is what
			PROVES the exception died, and a rule with no literal left is a rule that can no
			longer fail (SPEC V20).

			It reached zero by the tab moving to it, not by HEALTH moving: the left chain used to
			end at 891 and I125g measured that HEALTH's floor was 888 all along - 561 + 10*27 +
			57, a 27px track that follows no ruler of ours. T904 then moved the floor to 896 by
			taking HEALTH_BOX_PAD from 57 to 65, because the VIRTUES + ROAD stack needed 335 in a
			band of 327 and both boxes were already at their own minimum (SPEC I134m, B125).
			Below the floor the sign of V69 FLIPS and HEALTH starts overhanging instead of
			falling short, which is a different box and not what that rule was written to
			tolerate.

			Label widths are sized for the LONGER of [en] and [pt]: "Animal Ken" is
			"Empatia com Animais" (19 chars) in pt, so the ability label is 135px, not 80.
			It was 125 until the 49th round, when the ABILITIES frame came off and handed the
			three columns 10px apiece: the point of that request was the names, so the width
			went to the label and the dots moved right with it (SPEC T408, V170).

			Ability / CustomAbility put their first dot at x=135 and Attribute at x=125. V26
			compares rows that are SIBLINGS, and those two never share a box, so each column
			still lines up with itself. Advantages / Willpower carry no label and start at
			x=0 - they live alone in their own box and are centred by the caller.
		-->
		<!-- The input sits at 132, not 112, and the 20px before it is the ? COLUMN: nature and
		     demeanor draw a ? there (T846, I102h) and concept - a typed field - leaves it empty,
		     exactly as MeritFree leaves the slot MeritPicked fills (SPEC I102f). V26 compares
		     SIBLINGS, and left=326 holds two HeaderPicker rows and one Header, so the gap has to
		     exist in BOTH templates or the column stops lining up (SPEC V26, B12). The label keeps
		     its 105 - that width is what `Comportamento` needs in pt, and the 20 came out of the
		     input, which had 215 for a field nobody fills to the edge. -->
		<template name="Header">
			<label left="0" top="5" width="105" height="20" text="$(nome)" horzTextAlign="trailing"/>
			<edit left="132" top="0" width="195" height="25" field="$(field)"/>
		</template>
		<!-- Same row, shorter label. The 105px of `Header` is what `Demeanor` needs in pt
		     ("Comportamento", ~86px) and Demeanor lives in the middle column - keeping that
		     width in the first one is what pushed Nome / Jogador / Cronica to the right.
		     Here the longest pt label is "Jogador", so 75 is room to spare (SPEC V16/V25).
		     V26 compares rows that share a `left`, i.e. rows of the same column, so columns
		     may carry different label widths; all three rows of column one use this one. -->
		<template name="HeaderNarrow">
			<label left="0" top="5" width="75" height="20" text="$(nome)" horzTextAlign="trailing"/>
			<edit left="82" top="0" width="215" height="25" field="$(field)"/>
		</template>
		<template name="HeaderPicker">
			<label left="0" top="5" width="105" height="20" text="$(nome)" horzTextAlign="trailing"/>
			<button name="btnQ$(field)" left="108" top="0" width="20" height="20" text="?" onClick="popOpen(self, 'Nature', sheet['$(field)'], nil, '$(field)');"/>
			<button name="dyn$(field)" left="132" top="0" width="195" height="25" text="Select $(nome)" onClick="mfOpen(self, '$(field)', '$(field)', 'Nature');" onMenu="mfMenuOpen('$(field)', '$(field)');"/>
			<edit name="edt$(field)" left="132" top="0" width="195" height="25" field="$(field)" visible="false" enabled="false"/>
		</template>
		<!-- The ! of a trait opens its specialities (SPEC I172c/d, V504). It sits LEFT of the dots,
		     5 before the first one, and the label gave the room up: the dots do not move, so every
		     column still lines up (SPEC V26). Every ! hands over the field of its row's FIRST dot
		     and specOpen drops the "_1" - here dot 1 is a fixed image with no field, so the
		     '$(field)_1' is only that convention (SPEC I172c). The three Virtues used this template
		     and get no ! : they have one of their own, Virtue, which is this row as it was. -->
		<template name="Virtue">
			<button name="btnQ$(field)" left="0" top="0" width="20" height="20" text="?" onClick="popOpen(self, 'Virtue', virtueName('$(field)'));"/>
			<label left="25" top="5" width="135" height="20" text="$(nome)"/>
			<image left="165" top="0" width="25" height="25" style="autoFit" src="images/prime_on.png"/>
			<imageCheckBox left="190" top="0" width="25" height="25" field="$(field)_2" checkedImage="images/prime_on.png" uncheckedImage="images/prime_off.png" autoChange="false" onClick="xpClick('$(field)_2', self);"/>
			<imageCheckBox left="215" top="0" width="25" height="25" field="$(field)_3" checkedImage="images/prime_on.png" uncheckedImage="images/prime_off.png" autoChange="false" onClick="xpClick('$(field)_3', self);"/>
			<imageCheckBox left="240" top="0" width="25" height="25" field="$(field)_4" checkedImage="images/prime_on.png" uncheckedImage="images/prime_off.png" autoChange="false" onClick="xpClick('$(field)_4', self);"/>
			<imageCheckBox left="265" top="0" width="25" height="25" field="$(field)_5" checkedImage="images/prime_on.png" uncheckedImage="images/prime_off.png" autoChange="false" onClick="xpClick('$(field)_5', self);"/>
		</template>
		<!-- The two Virtues a Road can replace (SPEC I250b): the same row with a picker where Virtue
		     has its label. The dots keep the field they always had, so no sheet has to migrate; the
		     NAME lives in $(field)Name and renderVirtueButtons paints it through virtueName.
		     dynName is that label, for a Road that dictates the Virtue: renderVirtueButtons shows it
		     or the button, never both (SPEC I252a/b, V595). -->
		<template name="VirtuePicker">
			<button name="btnQ$(field)" left="0" top="0" width="20" height="20" text="?" onClick="popOpen(self, 'Virtue', virtueName('$(field)'), nil, '$(field)Name');"/>
			<label name="dynName$(field)" left="25" top="5" width="135" height="20" text="$(nome)" visible="false"/>
			<button name="dyn$(field)" left="25" top="0" width="135" height="25" text="$(nome)" onClick="mfOpen(self, '$(field)Name', '$(list)', 'Virtue');"/>
			<edit name="edt$(field)" left="25" top="0" width="135" height="25" field="$(field)Name" visible="false" enabled="false"/>
			<image left="165" top="0" width="25" height="25" style="autoFit" src="images/prime_on.png"/>
			<imageCheckBox left="190" top="0" width="25" height="25" field="$(field)_2" checkedImage="images/prime_on.png" uncheckedImage="images/prime_off.png" autoChange="false" onClick="xpClick('$(field)_2', self);"/>
			<imageCheckBox left="215" top="0" width="25" height="25" field="$(field)_3" checkedImage="images/prime_on.png" uncheckedImage="images/prime_off.png" autoChange="false" onClick="xpClick('$(field)_3', self);"/>
			<imageCheckBox left="240" top="0" width="25" height="25" field="$(field)_4" checkedImage="images/prime_on.png" uncheckedImage="images/prime_off.png" autoChange="false" onClick="xpClick('$(field)_4', self);"/>
			<imageCheckBox left="265" top="0" width="25" height="25" field="$(field)_5" checkedImage="images/prime_on.png" uncheckedImage="images/prime_off.png" autoChange="false" onClick="xpClick('$(field)_5', self);"/>
		</template>
		<!-- Two rectangles ride every row that has a ! (33rd batch). hit* is the FIRST child, behind
		     everything, filling the row's own layout - which runs from the name's start to the last
		     dot's end - so the tip shows on the name and on the 5px gaps too (SPEC I178e, V519).
		     blinkSp* sits right AFTER the !, over it, hidden and deaf to the mouse: the red that
		     specBangPaint and bangBlink flash while the ! is starred - a <button> has no
		     background colour of its own (SPEC I178b, V518, R178b). -->
		<!-- The numbers below are the MORTAL's. In a vampire's Main the root tightens each row - label 79,
		     ? and dots 16 to the left - through VAMP_GEOM (SPEC I202a, V546), so this template does not move. -->
		<template name="Attribute">
			<rectangle name="hit$(field)" align="contents" color="#00000000" strokeColor="#00000000" hitTest="true" onMouseMove="noteTipMove(self, event, 'spec', '$(field)_1', 'hit$(field)');" onMouseLeave="noteTipLeave(self);"/>
			<label name="lbl$(field)" left="0" top="5" width="95" height="20" text="$(nome)" onMouseMove="noteTipMove(self, event, 'spec', '$(field)_1', 'lbl$(field)');" onMouseLeave="noteTipLeave(self);"/>
			<button name="btnSp$(field)" left="100" top="2" width="20" height="20" text="!" fontColor="white" onClick="specOpen(self, '$(field)_1');" onMouseMove="noteTipMove(self, event, 'spec', '$(field)_1', 'btnSp$(field)');" onMouseLeave="noteTipLeave(self);"/>
			<rectangle name="blinkSp$(field)" left="100" top="2" width="20" height="20" color="#99D32F2F" strokeColor="#00000000" hitTest="false" visible="false"/>
			<image name="dot$(field)_1" left="125" top="0" width="25" height="25" style="autoFit" src="images/prime_on.png" onMouseMove="noteTipMove(self, event, 'spec', '$(field)_1', 'dot$(field)_1');" onMouseLeave="noteTipLeave(self);"/>
			<imageCheckBox name="dot$(field)_2" left="150" top="0" width="25" height="25" field="$(field)_2" checkedImage="images/prime_on.png" uncheckedImage="images/prime_off.png" autoChange="false" onClick="xpClick('$(field)_2', self);" onMouseMove="noteTipMove(self, event, 'spec', '$(field)_1', 'dot$(field)_2');" onMouseLeave="noteTipLeave(self);"/>
			<imageCheckBox name="dot$(field)_3" left="175" top="0" width="25" height="25" field="$(field)_3" checkedImage="images/prime_on.png" uncheckedImage="images/prime_off.png" autoChange="false" onClick="xpClick('$(field)_3', self);" onMouseMove="noteTipMove(self, event, 'spec', '$(field)_1', 'dot$(field)_3');" onMouseLeave="noteTipLeave(self);"/>
			<imageCheckBox name="dot$(field)_4" left="200" top="0" width="25" height="25" field="$(field)_4" checkedImage="images/prime_on.png" uncheckedImage="images/prime_off.png" autoChange="false" onClick="xpClick('$(field)_4', self);" onMouseMove="noteTipMove(self, event, 'spec', '$(field)_1', 'dot$(field)_4');" onMouseLeave="noteTipLeave(self);"/>
			<imageCheckBox name="dot$(field)_5" left="225" top="0" width="25" height="25" field="$(field)_5" checkedImage="images/prime_on.png" uncheckedImage="images/prime_off.png" autoChange="false" onClick="xpClick('$(field)_5', self);" onMouseMove="noteTipMove(self, event, 'spec', '$(field)_1', 'dot$(field)_5');" onMouseLeave="noteTipLeave(self);"/>
			<imageCheckBox name="dot$(field)_6" left="250" top="0" width="25" height="25" field="$(field)_6" checkedImage="images/prime_on.png" uncheckedImage="images/prime_off.png" autoChange="false" onClick="xpClick('$(field)_6', self);" onMouseMove="noteTipMove(self, event, 'spec', '$(field)_1', 'dot$(field)_6');" onMouseLeave="noteTipLeave(self);" visible="false"/>
			<imageCheckBox name="dot$(field)_7" left="275" top="0" width="25" height="25" field="$(field)_7" checkedImage="images/prime_on.png" uncheckedImage="images/prime_off.png" autoChange="false" onClick="xpClick('$(field)_7', self);" onMouseMove="noteTipMove(self, event, 'spec', '$(field)_1', 'dot$(field)_7');" onMouseLeave="noteTipLeave(self);" visible="false"/>
			<imageCheckBox name="dot$(field)_8" left="300" top="0" width="25" height="25" field="$(field)_8" checkedImage="images/prime_on.png" uncheckedImage="images/prime_off.png" autoChange="false" onClick="xpClick('$(field)_8', self);" onMouseMove="noteTipMove(self, event, 'spec', '$(field)_1', 'dot$(field)_8');" onMouseLeave="noteTipLeave(self);" visible="false"/>
			<imageCheckBox name="dot$(field)_9" left="325" top="0" width="25" height="25" field="$(field)_9" checkedImage="images/prime_on.png" uncheckedImage="images/prime_off.png" autoChange="false" onClick="xpClick('$(field)_9', self);" onMouseMove="noteTipMove(self, event, 'spec', '$(field)_1', 'dot$(field)_9');" onMouseLeave="noteTipLeave(self);" visible="false"/>
			<imageCheckBox name="dot$(field)_10" left="350" top="0" width="25" height="25" field="$(field)_10" checkedImage="images/prime_on.png" uncheckedImage="images/prime_off.png" autoChange="false" onClick="xpClick('$(field)_10', self);" onMouseMove="noteTipMove(self, event, 'spec', '$(field)_1', 'dot$(field)_10');" onMouseLeave="noteTipLeave(self);" visible="false"/>
			<imageCheckBox name="mcap$(field)_4" left="200" top="0" width="25" height="25" checked="false" checkedImage="images/prime_on.png" uncheckedImage="images/prime_off.png" autoChange="false" opacity="0.30" visible="false"/>
			<imageCheckBox name="mcap$(field)_5" left="225" top="0" width="25" height="25" checked="false" checkedImage="images/prime_on.png" uncheckedImage="images/prime_off.png" autoChange="false" opacity="0.30" visible="false"/>
			<imageCheckBox name="mcap$(field)_6" left="250" top="0" width="25" height="25" checked="false" checkedImage="images/prime_on.png" uncheckedImage="images/prime_off.png" autoChange="false" opacity="0.30" visible="false"/>
			<imageCheckBox name="mcap$(field)_7" left="275" top="0" width="25" height="25" checked="false" checkedImage="images/prime_on.png" uncheckedImage="images/prime_off.png" autoChange="false" opacity="0.30" visible="false"/>
			<imageCheckBox name="mcap$(field)_8" left="300" top="0" width="25" height="25" checked="false" checkedImage="images/prime_on.png" uncheckedImage="images/prime_off.png" autoChange="false" opacity="0.30" visible="false"/>
			<imageCheckBox name="mcap$(field)_9" left="325" top="0" width="25" height="25" checked="false" checkedImage="images/prime_on.png" uncheckedImage="images/prime_off.png" autoChange="false" opacity="0.30" visible="false"/>
			<imageCheckBox name="mcap$(field)_10" left="350" top="0" width="25" height="25" checked="false" checkedImage="images/prime_on.png" uncheckedImage="images/prime_off.png" autoChange="false" opacity="0.30" visible="false"/>
		</template>
		<!-- Attribute, but dot 1 is a real checkbox instead of a fixed image, so the rating can
		     drop to zero. Only Appearance uses it (SPEC T95). -->
		<template name="AttributeZeroable">
			<rectangle name="hit$(field)" align="contents" color="#00000000" strokeColor="#00000000" hitTest="true" onMouseMove="noteTipMove(self, event, 'spec', '$(field)_1', 'hit$(field)');" onMouseLeave="noteTipLeave(self);"/>
			<label name="lbl$(field)" left="0" top="5" width="95" height="20" text="$(nome)" onMouseMove="noteTipMove(self, event, 'spec', '$(field)_1', 'lbl$(field)');" onMouseLeave="noteTipLeave(self);"/>
			<button name="btnSp$(field)" left="100" top="2" width="20" height="20" text="!" fontColor="white" onClick="specOpen(self, '$(field)_1');" onMouseMove="noteTipMove(self, event, 'spec', '$(field)_1', 'btnSp$(field)');" onMouseLeave="noteTipLeave(self);"/>
			<rectangle name="blinkSp$(field)" left="100" top="2" width="20" height="20" color="#99D32F2F" strokeColor="#00000000" hitTest="false" visible="false"/>
			<imageCheckBox name="dot$(field)_1" left="125" top="0" width="25" height="25" field="$(field)_1" checkedImage="images/prime_on.png" uncheckedImage="images/prime_off.png" autoChange="false" onClick="xpClick('$(field)_1', self);" onMouseMove="noteTipMove(self, event, 'spec', '$(field)_1', 'dot$(field)_1');" onMouseLeave="noteTipLeave(self);"/>
			<imageCheckBox name="dot$(field)_2" left="150" top="0" width="25" height="25" field="$(field)_2" checkedImage="images/prime_on.png" uncheckedImage="images/prime_off.png" autoChange="false" onClick="xpClick('$(field)_2', self);" onMouseMove="noteTipMove(self, event, 'spec', '$(field)_1', 'dot$(field)_2');" onMouseLeave="noteTipLeave(self);"/>
