		</layout>

		<layout name="boxKnowledges" left="1015" top="110" width="330" height="426">
			<rectangle align="client" color="black" xradius="14" yradius="14" cornerType="innerRound"/>
			<label left="20" top="15" width="290" height="20" text="KNOWLEDGES" horzTextAlign="center" anchors="left top right"/>

			<layout left="20" top="36" width="290" height="25" anchors="left top right" >
				<Ability col="knowledges" num="1" field="academics" nome="Academics"/>
			</layout>
			<layout left="20" top="61" width="290" height="25" anchors="left top right" >
				<Ability col="knowledges" num="2" field="cosmology" nome="Cosmology"/>
			</layout>
			<layout left="20" top="86" width="290" height="25" anchors="left top right" >
				<Ability col="knowledges" num="3" field="enigmas" nome="Enigmas"/>
			</layout>
			<layout left="20" top="111" width="290" height="25" anchors="left top right" >
				<Ability col="knowledges" num="4" field="esoterica" nome="Esoterica"/>
			</layout>
			<layout left="20" top="136" width="290" height="25" anchors="left top right" >
				<Ability col="knowledges" num="5" field="finance" nome="Finance"/>
			</layout>
			<layout left="20" top="161" width="290" height="25" anchors="left top right" >
				<Ability col="knowledges" num="6" field="investigation" nome="Investigation"/>
			</layout>
			<layout left="20" top="186" width="290" height="25" anchors="left top right" >
				<Ability col="knowledges" num="7" field="law" nome="Law"/>
			</layout>
			<layout left="20" top="211" width="290" height="25" anchors="left top right" >
				<Ability col="knowledges" num="8" field="medicine" nome="Medicine"/>
			</layout>
			<layout left="20" top="236" width="290" height="25" anchors="left top right" >
				<Ability col="knowledges" num="9" field="occult" nome="Occult"/>
			</layout>
			<layout left="20" top="261" width="290" height="25" anchors="left top right" >
				<Ability col="knowledges" num="10" field="politics" nome="Politics"/>
			</layout>
			<layout name="dynAbilRow_knowledges_11" left="20" top="286" width="290" height="25" anchors="left top right" >
				<Ability col="knowledges" num="11" field="science" nome="Science"/>
			</layout>
			<layout name="dynAbilFill_knowledges_11" visible="false" left="20" top="286" width="290" height="25" anchors="left top right" >
				<CustomAbility field="customKnowledge_4"/>
			</layout>
			<layout name="dynAbilRow_knowledges_12" left="20" top="311" width="290" height="25" anchors="left top right" >
				<Ability col="knowledges" num="12" field="technology" nome="Technology"/>
			</layout>
			<layout name="dynAbilFill_knowledges_12" visible="false" left="20" top="311" width="290" height="25" anchors="left top right" >
				<CustomAbility field="customKnowledge_5"/>
			</layout>
			<!--
				The thirteenth knowledge and a typed row on ONE top, and the renderer shows exactly
				one of them (SPEC I123b, V371b). Knowledges is the only column an era changes the
				length of: Modern Nights and the Classical Age list thirteen, the Victorian era and
				the Dark Ages twelve. An era borrows a trait from no other era (Q34), so the two
				short eras pay for the row with a name the player types instead.

				One top and not two: a second top would leave 25px of hole in whichever era hides
				the upper row, which is the gap this pairing exists to close. It is the hidden pair
				MeritPicked already runs (SPEC V354a), one row wider.

				Authored state is the Victorian era like every other row here (SPEC V76), so the
				named half ships hidden and the typed half ships visible. Its field is `computer`
				because that is the one knowledge no twelve-name era lists: the authored column
				stays one field per row even with the hidden one counted.
			-->
			<layout name="dynAbilRow_knowledges_13" visible="false" left="20" top="336" width="290" height="25" anchors="left top right" >
				<Ability col="knowledges" num="13" field="computer" nome="Computer"/>
			</layout>
			<layout name="dynAbilFill_knowledges_13" left="20" top="336" width="290" height="25" anchors="left top right" >
				<CustomAbility field="customKnowledge_3"/>
			</layout>
			<layout name="dynAbilTail_knowledges_14" left="20" top="361" width="290" height="25" anchors="left top right" >
				<CustomAbility field="customKnowledge_1"/>
			</layout>
			<layout name="dynAbilTail_knowledges_15" left="20" top="386" width="290" height="25" anchors="left top right" >
				<CustomAbility field="customKnowledge_2"/>
			</layout>
		</layout>

		<!--
			Bottom row since the 46th batch (SPEC I189c/d) - the map at the top of the file has
			the numbers: VIRTUES over ROAD + BEARING + WILLPOWER | BLOOD POOL | HEALTH.

			Every one of them takes its x from the column above it since the 50th round
			(SPEC V168, V375): VIRTUES and ROAD from TALENTS, BLOOD POOL from SKILLS (the place
			SPECIALTIES held until the 44th batch, and ROAD until the 46th), HEALTH from
			KNOWLEDGES. They rose 50 with the 50th
			round, which is what the ability columns gave back when they stopped carrying a
			black tail (SPEC V171).

			Virtues and Humanity are 290 wide, not 410: their content is a 250px track (a 125px
			label plus 5 dots, or 10 bare dots), so 410 left a wide empty margin and made the
			Humanity/Willpower dots read as right-aligned. 290 = 250 + a 20px margin each side,
			which centres both tracks. The 120px freed went to HEALTH.

			HEALTH is 290 wide because 150 was not enough for its own labels: "Wounded (-2)" is
			"Ferido Gravemente (-2)" in pt, ~143px in a 125px checkBox. V16 only measures
			<label>, never <checkBox>, so that overflow was never flagged by the gate.

			Faith is gone from this tab on purpose: `faith_1`..`_5` are now the dots of the
			TRUE FAITH row on the Powers tab, so a saved sheet keeps its rating (SPEC V35).
		-->
		<layout name="boxVirtues" left="345" top="541" width="330" height="126">
			<rectangle align="client" color="black" xradius="14" yradius="14" cornerType="innerRound"/>
			<label left="20" top="15" width="290" height="20" text="VIRTUES" horzTextAlign="center" anchors="left top right"/>

			<!-- Named for a vampire (SPEC I193d, V537a): there the box is 340 wide, under TALENTS,
			     and VAMP_GEOM re-centres the three rows - a fixed child left behind in a box that
			     changes shape is B191. -->
			<layout name="virtueRow_conscience" left="20" top="36" width="290" height="25" >
				<VirtuePicker field="conscience" list="virtue1" nome="Conscience"/>
			</layout>
			<layout name="virtueRow_selfControl" left="20" top="61" width="290" height="25" >
				<VirtuePicker field="selfControl" list="virtue2" nome="Self-Control"/>
			</layout>
			<layout name="virtueRow_courage" left="20" top="86" width="290" height="25" >
				<Virtue field="courage" nome="Courage"/>
			</layout>
		</layout>

		<!-- Between VIRTUES and HEALTH, under SKILLS, for a mortal (47th batch, SPEC I190a, user
		     2026-10-01) - where the 44th batch had put it. A vampire's BLOOD POOL needs that band, so
		     for a vampire renderGameMode moves this box to 345..675 instead (VAMP_GEOM, SPEC V534c):
		     the box keeps its size and its children, only left/top move. Since the 50th batch it is
		     not stacked under VIRTUES any more - VIRTUES went under TALENTS - and closes up on the
		     abilities (SPEC I193e).

		     Since the 52nd batch (user 2026-10-02, SPEC I195, V541) ROAD holds the road alone and
		     WILLPOWER is boxWillpower under it, in BOTH games: the two together are as tall as the
		     Main's BLOOD POOL box (126 + 5 + 113 = 244), so a mortal's close on HEALTH's seven-level
		     line with the avatar and a vampire's with the pool. Since the 56th batch (user 2026-10-02,
		     SPEC I199a, V541a) ROAD is as tall as VIRTUES beside it, and WILLPOWER paid the 4.

		     Inside (56th batch, SPEC I199b, V541c): the dots sit at the box's vertical CENTRE, 50
		     above and 51 under (the odd pixel under, SPEC V399), and the picker line and the bearing
		     line come in to 6 of them - half the 11 / 12 the 53rd batch spaced them by. -->
		<layout name="boxRoad" left="680" top="541" width="330" height="126">
			<rectangle align="client" color="black" xradius="14" yradius="14" cornerType="innerRound"/>

			<!--
				HUMANITY became ROAD in the 125th round (SPEC I99a). Only the LABEL moved: the ten
				dots are still `humanity_1`..`_10`, so a saved sheet keeps its rating (SPEC V2, V5) -
				the same trade `retainers`->GUIDES and `items`->TRANSPORTATION already made.

				`cboRoad` sits ABOVE the track, so the box title says what the track IS and the combo
				says WHICH road. It leads on `Humanity` and carries no empty item: a character with no
				road IS on Humanity, which is the V15 exception SPEC C declares (SPEC I99b).

				The bearing line is glued to the bottom of the dots at top=99 - the dots close exactly
				there - because the request asked for it with no gap. Two labels and not one padded
				string: V11 forbids padding to line a column up, and the modifier is its own column
				(SPEC I99e). They carry the `dyn` prefix and NO text=: that prefix is what keeps the
				WoD20.6 language traversal off a Lua-written label, which would otherwise snapshot the
				authored English and restore it stale (SPEC V31) - the same reason the health rows use
				it. SPEC I99e names them lbl*, and that spelling is wrong for a Lua-written label.

				cboRoad is 290 and not 250: the ruler wants 241px for `The Path of Power and the Inner
				Voice` plus the 24px arrow (SPEC V312), so the dot track's width would clip it. It
				spans the box interior instead.

				WILLPOWER fell 49 and the box grew 26 to fit, which is the second branch the user chose
				in Q8. SPECIALTIES and the avatar grew the SAME 26 in the same commit - V69 reads all
				three closing on one y, and moving one alone turns it red (SPEC I99i, I99j).
			-->
			<!-- The pair is CENTRED as a group, and the group's width moves with the language:
			     `ROAD` is four characters and `CAMINHO` is seven (SPEC I128b/I128c, V380, T864,
			     user 2026-08-31 ask 6). renderRoadPair writes both lefts and the label's width
			     from ROAD_LABEL_W at every language change.

			     What is AUTHORED here is the LONGER of the two - pt, 80px at left=30 - and not
			     the English the sheet is written in: V16/V25 and V351(c) read the XML, and a
			     label authored at the English width would be a clipped `CAMINHO` sitting in the
			     file waiting for someone to open the sheet in pt. Declaring the worst case and
			     letting the renderer shrink it is what HEALTH already does with its ten-row
			     height (SPEC V49) - the file says the biggest it can ever be, and Lua takes it
			     down. Nothing is measured against the English case except the screen. -->
			<label name="lblRoad" left="30" top="20" width="80" height="24" text="ROAD" horzTextAlign="trailing" vertTextAlign="center"/>
			<!-- The Classical Age calls this box PHILOSOPHY (SPEC I251). It is a label of
			     its own, authored at its widest case (en, 114) the way lblRoad authors pt;
			     renderRoadPair shows one of the two. -->
			<label name="lblPhilosophy" left="13" top="20" width="114" height="24" text="PHILOSOPHY" horzTextAlign="trailing" vertTextAlign="center" visible="false"/>
			<button name="btnQroad" left="115" top="20" width="20" height="24" text="?" onClick="popOpen(self, 'Road', sheet['road'], nil, 'road');"/>
			<button name="dynroad" left="140" top="20" width="160" height="24" fontSize="12" text="Select Road" onClick="mfOpen(self, 'road', 'road', 'Road');" onMenu="mfMenuOpen('road', 'road');"/>
			<!-- The typed twin, one field and two widgets with exactly one visible (SPEC I71, V274).
			     Authored state IS the flag off - visible AND enabled - because invisible-and-enabled
			     still takes Tab focus, which no screenshot shows (SPEC V274c, V274d). -->
			<edit name="edtRoad" left="140" top="20" width="160" height="24" field="road" visible="false" enabled="false"/>
			<layout left="40" top="50" width="250" height="25" >
				<Advantages field="humanity"/>
			</layout>
			<!-- ONE label and not two (user 2026-08-29): the bearing and its modifier read as a
			     single centred sentence, which two labels cannot do - each would centre in its own
			     half and the pair would drift off centre as the name grows. This REVOKES the
			     "the modifier is its own column" half of I99e; V11 is untouched, because what
			     joins them is a real space and a real parenthesis, not padding.
			
			     0.80 is neither of the two dimming numbers of I43/V244 and is not trying to be:
			     those two say "read-only", this one is the emphasis the user asked for on a line
			     that was never editable. Authored, so no runtime write reaches V244. -->
			<label name="dynBearingName" left="20" top="81" width="290" height="20" horzTextAlign="center" opacity="0.80"/>
		</layout>

		<!-- WILLPOWER, a box of its own under ROAD in every game since the 52nd batch (user 2026-10-02,
		     SPEC I195, V540, V541): the 51st had split it for a vampire only, with a second copy of the
		     row hidden inside ROAD for a mortal; once the mortal split too there was nothing left for
		     the copy to do, and this is again the ONE willpower row of the tab (SPEC V1). For a
		     vampire VAMP_GEOM moves it with ROAD. Title, dots and checkboxes: 8 from the title to the
		     dots and 2 from the dots to the checkboxes in the template - the user's 2px, the same on
		     the Combat tab and on the Vampire tab's copy (57th batch, user 2026-10-02, SPEC I200a,
		     V545a). The three are ONE object centred in the box since the 61st batch (user
		     2026-10-02, SPEC I204c, V547): 20 + 8 + 52 = 80 in the 113 of V541a, 16 above and 17 under. -->
		<!-- Title and body named in the 74th batch (user 2026-10-06, SPEC I217d): a MAGE's WILLPOWER
		     takes VIRTUES' 340 x 126 and MAGE_GEOM re-centres the two as one object. -->
		<layout name="boxWillpower" left="680" top="672" width="330" height="113">
			<rectangle align="client" color="black" xradius="14" yradius="14" cornerType="innerRound"/>
			<label name="lblWillpower" left="20" top="16" width="290" height="20" text="WILLPOWER" horzTextAlign="center"/>
			<layout name="bodyWillpower" left="40" top="44" width="250" height="52" >
				<Willpower field="willpower"/>
			</layout>
		</layout>

		<!-- A MAGE's Quintessence / Paradox wheel (user 2026-10-06, SPEC I218, V555), in the slot ROAD left
		     beside WILLPOWER: 200 x 244 since the 78th batch (SPEC I221b, V558b - the ring's 160 and 20 a
		     side; it was 330), WILLPOWER's top to EXPERIENCE's foot. Twenty marks on a circle of
		     radius 73 round (100, 122), one every 18 degrees from 171 (left, a touch up) clockwise to the
		     twentieth just under the first - Quintessence fills clockwise from 1, Paradox counter-
		     clockwise from 20. Each mark is Health's: a stroked square whose label carries the field, so
		     the NDB paints the symbol; 16 x 16 and not Health's 22 x 20: an upright square on the diagonal
		     of a circle this size needs 16 or less to clear its neighbour (SPEC B200). The
		     positions are generated (left = round(100 + 73 cos t) - 8, top = round(122 - 73 sin t) - 8, the
		     ring's own top taken off). The ring is a layout of its own: titles 15 from the edges (V240)
		     and the clickable marks off the box's ground rectangle (V68).
		     80th batch (user 2026-10-07, SPEC I223a/b, V562): the mark is PAINTED, not lettered - no label
		     child; renderQpWheel colours it gold for "/" and dark purple for "X". Each mark turns its
		     base to the ring's centre: rotationAngle = (18 N - 99) mod 360, generated; the host turns a
		     control about its own centre, so the positions above do not move (SPEC B61).
		     Hidden here: renderGameMode shows it to a mage only. Since the 95th batch (user 2026-10-08,
		     SPEC I238c, V579c) it swaps places with WILLPOWER: on the Main's left edge, under SPHERES. Since the
		     96th batch (user 2026-10-08, SPEC I239b, V580b) it is SPHERES' 370 wide and its five children
		     stand 85 right of the 200 they were drawn for, centred on 185. Since the 100th batch (user
		     2026-10-09, SPEC I243d, V584c) it stands 5 under ATTRIBUTES and is its 434 wide, the five
		     children 117 right of the 200, centred on 217. -->
		<layout name="boxQuintParadox" left="0" top="411" width="434" height="244" visible="false">
			<rectangle align="client" color="black" xradius="14" yradius="14" cornerType="innerRound"/>
			<!-- Each title shares its line with the number it names (user 2026-10-06, SPEC I219a): the
			     numbers are the truth and the ring draws them (renderQpWheel). Since the 77th batch
			     (SPEC I220, V557) the title is right-aligned and ends 5 before its number, and the pair
			     sits about the box's middle - centred on the pt name, the longer: QUINTESSENCIA ~98 +
			     5 + 40 = 143 from 29, PARADOXO ~60 + 5 + 40 = 105 from 47 (centre 100 since the 78th batch,
			     SPEC I221b). -->
			<label left="137" top="15" width="107" height="20" text="QUINTESSENCE" horzTextAlign="trailing"/>
			<edit name="edtQpQuint" field="qpQuint" type="number" decimalPlaces="0" left="249" top="15" width="40" height="20" horzTextAlign="center" vertTextAlign="center"/>
			<layout name="qpRing" left="137" top="42" width="160" height="160">
				<rectangle name="qpMark_1" left="0" top="61" width="16" height="16" color="#00000000" strokeColor="white" strokeSize="2" xradius="2" yradius="2" rotationAngle="279" hitTest="true" cursor="handPoint" onClick="cycleQpMark(1);"/>
				<rectangle name="qpMark_2" left="7" top="39" width="16" height="16" color="#00000000" strokeColor="white" strokeSize="2" xradius="2" yradius="2" rotationAngle="297" hitTest="true" cursor="handPoint" onClick="cycleQpMark(2);"/>
				<rectangle name="qpMark_3" left="20" top="20" width="16" height="16" color="#00000000" strokeColor="white" strokeSize="2" xradius="2" yradius="2" rotationAngle="315" hitTest="true" cursor="handPoint" onClick="cycleQpMark(3);"/>
				<rectangle name="qpMark_4" left="39" top="7" width="16" height="16" color="#00000000" strokeColor="white" strokeSize="2" xradius="2" yradius="2" rotationAngle="333" hitTest="true" cursor="handPoint" onClick="cycleQpMark(4);"/>
				<rectangle name="qpMark_5" left="61" top="0" width="16" height="16" color="#00000000" strokeColor="white" strokeSize="2" xradius="2" yradius="2" rotationAngle="351" hitTest="true" cursor="handPoint" onClick="cycleQpMark(5);"/>
				<rectangle name="qpMark_6" left="83" top="0" width="16" height="16" color="#00000000" strokeColor="white" strokeSize="2" xradius="2" yradius="2" rotationAngle="9" hitTest="true" cursor="handPoint" onClick="cycleQpMark(6);"/>
				<rectangle name="qpMark_7" left="105" top="7" width="16" height="16" color="#00000000" strokeColor="white" strokeSize="2" xradius="2" yradius="2" rotationAngle="27" hitTest="true" cursor="handPoint" onClick="cycleQpMark(7);"/>
				<rectangle name="qpMark_8" left="124" top="20" width="16" height="16" color="#00000000" strokeColor="white" strokeSize="2" xradius="2" yradius="2" rotationAngle="45" hitTest="true" cursor="handPoint" onClick="cycleQpMark(8);"/>
				<rectangle name="qpMark_9" left="137" top="39" width="16" height="16" color="#00000000" strokeColor="white" strokeSize="2" xradius="2" yradius="2" rotationAngle="63" hitTest="true" cursor="handPoint" onClick="cycleQpMark(9);"/>
				<rectangle name="qpMark_10" left="144" top="61" width="16" height="16" color="#00000000" strokeColor="white" strokeSize="2" xradius="2" yradius="2" rotationAngle="81" hitTest="true" cursor="handPoint" onClick="cycleQpMark(10);"/>
				<rectangle name="qpMark_11" left="144" top="83" width="16" height="16" color="#00000000" strokeColor="white" strokeSize="2" xradius="2" yradius="2" rotationAngle="99" hitTest="true" cursor="handPoint" onClick="cycleQpMark(11);"/>
				<rectangle name="qpMark_12" left="137" top="105" width="16" height="16" color="#00000000" strokeColor="white" strokeSize="2" xradius="2" yradius="2" rotationAngle="117" hitTest="true" cursor="handPoint" onClick="cycleQpMark(12);"/>
				<rectangle name="qpMark_13" left="124" top="124" width="16" height="16" color="#00000000" strokeColor="white" strokeSize="2" xradius="2" yradius="2" rotationAngle="135" hitTest="true" cursor="handPoint" onClick="cycleQpMark(13);"/>
				<rectangle name="qpMark_14" left="105" top="137" width="16" height="16" color="#00000000" strokeColor="white" strokeSize="2" xradius="2" yradius="2" rotationAngle="153" hitTest="true" cursor="handPoint" onClick="cycleQpMark(14);"/>
				<rectangle name="qpMark_15" left="83" top="144" width="16" height="16" color="#00000000" strokeColor="white" strokeSize="2" xradius="2" yradius="2" rotationAngle="171" hitTest="true" cursor="handPoint" onClick="cycleQpMark(15);"/>
				<rectangle name="qpMark_16" left="61" top="144" width="16" height="16" color="#00000000" strokeColor="white" strokeSize="2" xradius="2" yradius="2" rotationAngle="189" hitTest="true" cursor="handPoint" onClick="cycleQpMark(16);"/>
				<rectangle name="qpMark_17" left="39" top="137" width="16" height="16" color="#00000000" strokeColor="white" strokeSize="2" xradius="2" yradius="2" rotationAngle="207" hitTest="true" cursor="handPoint" onClick="cycleQpMark(17);"/>
				<rectangle name="qpMark_18" left="20" top="124" width="16" height="16" color="#00000000" strokeColor="white" strokeSize="2" xradius="2" yradius="2" rotationAngle="225" hitTest="true" cursor="handPoint" onClick="cycleQpMark(18);"/>
				<rectangle name="qpMark_19" left="7" top="105" width="16" height="16" color="#00000000" strokeColor="white" strokeSize="2" xradius="2" yradius="2" rotationAngle="243" hitTest="true" cursor="handPoint" onClick="cycleQpMark(19);"/>
				<rectangle name="qpMark_20" left="0" top="83" width="16" height="16" color="#00000000" strokeColor="white" strokeSize="2" xradius="2" yradius="2" rotationAngle="261" hitTest="true" cursor="handPoint" onClick="cycleQpMark(20);"/>
			</layout>
			<label left="137" top="209" width="87" height="20" text="PARADOX" horzTextAlign="trailing"/>
			<edit name="edtQpParadox" field="qpParadox" type="number" decimalPlaces="0" left="229" top="209" width="40" height="20" horzTextAlign="center" vertTextAlign="center"/>
		</layout>

		<!-- ARETE over SPHERES, a MAGE's alone (user 2026-10-06, SPEC I221c, V559, V560): the slot between
		     the wheel and HEALTH, 664 x 244 since the 80th batch (SPEC I223f) - the wheel's height, the "double box". Two boxes
		     since the 82nd batch (user 2026-10-07, SPEC I225e, V567e): ARETE 89 over SPHERES 150, 5 between. Arete's first dot is
		     a fixed image, as a Virtue's (it starts at 1); the nine after it buy with XP. Since the 80th
		     batch (user 2026-10-07, SPEC I223e/f, Q137.1b, V564) a sphere row is an ability's: body font
		     and 25px dots. Each column is as wide as its longest name (98, 46, 59 by the gate's ruler) +
		     2 + 125 = 225, 173, 186, and the four gaps - edge, between, between, edge - are 20 each, which
		     is what closes the bottom row on 1375 with HEALTH at 206. Each dot from the 2nd has a
		     faded EMPTY twin (scap_) for the levels over Arete, the mcap pair of the attributes, swapped
		     by renderSpheres (SPEC I221j). Hidden here: renderGameMode shows it to a mage only. Since the 90th batch (user 2026-10-08,
		     SPEC I233b, V574b) the two stack under WILLPOWER right of KNOWLEDGES, 1005 to ATTRIBUTES' edge at 1375 (370),
		     and the nine spheres are ONE column: every name 98 wide, the row 225 centred at 72, 25 a row from 44 (30 until the 92nd batch, SPEC I235b - the abilities' step). Since
		     the 91st batch (SPEC I234c) WILLPOWER is back under TALENTS and the two rise to KNOWLEDGES' top. Since the 93rd batch
		     (user 2026-10-08, SPEC I236a, V577) ARETE is 81 (the track at 41, 15 under it - SPEC V240) so SPHERES closes on 617,
		     the foot of TALENTS and SKILLS in every era. Since the 95th batch (user 2026-10-08, SPEC I238b, V579b)
		     the two stand on the Main's left edge, before TALENTS. Since the 100th batch (user 2026-10-09,
		     SPEC I243d, V584c) they part: ARETE 5 under WILLPOWER and its 290 wide (the track 20 a side),
		     SPHERES between WILLPOWER and HEALTH, its right edge on SKILLS'. -->
		<layout name="boxArete" left="439" top="622" width="290" height="81" visible="false">
			<rectangle align="client" color="black" xradius="14" yradius="14" cornerType="innerRound"/>
